  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1053 PM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nThe upper level pattern is not expected to change much this week \nwith ridge centered to our east and westerlies remaining to the \nnorth, resulting in several more days of summer weather. Surface \nboundary lingering across the Central Plains remains just close \nenough that some associated convection could brush northern areas\na time or two, along with above mentioned possibility of \nisolated, mainly terrain-deriven convection each afternoon. But \nthe main message will be well above normal temperatures and \nlikely need for additional heat headlines. \n\nConsiderable uncertainty remains as to just when this pattern may\nfinally break down and allow for a frontal passage. Extended \nforecast continues to reflect a cooling trend with more meaningful\nrain chances early next week, but spread in guidance remains \nconsiderable in that range.",
